<title>INDIA: Indian soybean, meal, oil down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean, meal, oil down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were bearish in central Indian markets on limited demand from processing plants. Prices were down by 150-200 rupees per tonne. Around 80 percent of soybean sowing has been completed in central India, covering an area of 3.2 million hectares.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices remained down. Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 200 rupees per tonne. The undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were bearish. Soymeal yellow was $262-263 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) at west Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $94-96 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,200-3,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
